 4. 🐋 1 for the road: A new hope 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: The Center for Whale Research/NMFS/NOAA A new baby orca is making waves among the Pacific Northwest's endangered Southern Resident population, Axios Seattle's Christine Clarridge reports. 

 The little guy is the newest offspring of orca J35, who made headlines in 2018 while carrying her dead calf on her head for 17 days. 🐳 Researchers with the Center for Whale Research spotted the newborn swimming alongside his mother Monday and again on Tuesday.

 He appears to be nursing, swimming and socializing well. Go deeper ... Get Axios Local . 

 
 
